more than three weeks before Christmas  American Airlines faces a holiday  meltdown a union blames a computer  glitch for giving too many pilots time  off that scheduling mistake could leave  15,000 upcoming flights without a  captain copilot or both and those jets  cannot leave without them Kris Van  Cleave is at the American counter at  Reagan National Airport outside  Washington with the frustration that's  taking off Chris good morning good  morning this software issue could affect  flights between December 17th and the  31st and American is the world's largest  airline so this could have ripple  effects across the country but  particularly in hub cities like New York  Chicago Miami and here in Washington  American says they are working to solve  this problem the pilots union says that  might not be so easy  thousands of holiday travelers are  hoping for a Christmas miracle after the  union representing American Airlines  fifteen thousand pilots warned a looming  pilot shortage could ground flights  around the country it's super stressful  I mean when your flight plans don't work  out you're kind of left stranded it's  not fair and who's gonna fly us home  into our families you know Henry Hart a  belt is an airline analyst this was a  terrible screw-up by American Airlines  it was a programming mistake pilots  normally bid for flight assignments  every month the computer glitch allowed  them to drop their scheduled flights  during the holidays without confirming  another pilot was available as a result  thousands of flights were left unstaffed  American declined to go on camera saying  in a statement we have reserved pilots  to help cover and we are paying pilots  who pick up certain open trips 150  percent of their hourly rate obviously  American does not want to be the airline  equivalent of Scrooge and canceled a lot  of people's vacations still the pilots  union has lodged a protest against the  airline's proposed fix saying it's terms  violate the current labor contract  captain Dennis pagers it's gonna require  some unique thinking and some unusual  arrangements perhaps but none of that  can happen until we are actually able to  sit down and talk about it now American  says it does not intend to cancel any  flights during the holidays and believes  it can fill this pilot void in the  coming days airline analysts say passing  it is not time to panic just yet but  they can't rule out the possibility of  at least some cancellations so Nora will  be watching this closely just a small  panic going on if you have an American  ticket thank you Chris
 

